    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v2
      - name: Set up Node.js
        uses: actions/setup-node@v1
        with:
          node-version: '14'
      - name: Install dependencies
        run: npm install
      - name: Build and test
        run: npm run build && npm run test
```
This is a simple workflow for building and testing a project using GitHub Actions. It defines two jobs:

- `build`: This job runs when there's a new commit to the repository. It sets up Node.js, installs dependencies, builds the project, and tests it.
- `test`: This job runs when there's a pull request to the repository. It builds the project again and runs the tests.

The workflow also includes a step called "runs-on" which specifies the operating system (in this case, Ubuntu) that the job should run on. The "steps" section contains the actual code that the job does. In this case, it sets up Node.js, installs dependencies, builds the project, and tests it. Finally, it runs the tests again after the build has been completed.

