2. Be patient: Sometimes people need time to process their emotions. Don't push them too hard; instead, allow yourself to feel what they are feeling without judgment.

3. Focus on the positive: Even if your friend is being difficult, try to focus on the good times and how much fun you are having together. This will help diffuse the tension and make the situation less stressful.

4. Ask questions: If possible, ask your friend why they are being so negative and what they think they are missing out on. This might help clarify things and show them that you care about their well-being.

5. Find common ground: Try to find areas where both of you can agree on something. For example, maybe you both enjoy hiking in the same area, or going to the same restaurants.

6. Consider alternative options: If there are other activities you would like to do during your trip, consider exploring other destinations or finding ways to spend more time with your friends.

