                dp[i][j] = dp[i-1][j-1] + 1
            else:
                dp[i][j] = max(dp[i-1][j], dp[i][j-1])

    # The length of the longest common subsequence is stored in the bottom-right corner of the matrix
    return dp[m][n]
```

This function takes two input strings `str1` and `str2`, and returns the length of the longest common subsequence between them. It uses dynamic programming to build up the solution in a bottom-up manner, storing only the necessary values in a 2D array. 

The time complexity of this algorithm is O(mn), where m and n are the lengths of the input strings. This is because we need to compare each character of one string with every character of the other string exactly once.

