Then, we iterate through the strings from left to right and update the values of `dp` accordingly. For each position `(i, j)` in the strings, if the characters at positions `i-1` and `j-1` are equal, then `dp[i][j] = dp[i-1][j-1] + 1`. Otherwise, `dp[i][j] = max(dp[i-1][j], dp[i][j-1])`.

Finally, we return the value of `dp[m][n]`, where `m` and `n` are the lengths of the two input strings. This will give us the length of the LCS between the two strings.
